# Media Player Development Patterns

## State Management
- `PlayerService` is the canonical owner of playback state; use [apps/web/src/lib/effect/player-service.ts](mdc:apps/web/src/lib/effect/player-service.ts)
- Read playback state and issue commands through [apps/web/src/lib/effect/player-atoms.ts](mdc:apps/web/src/lib/effect/player-atoms.ts)
- `WatchTogetherSession` owns canonical session runtime state in [apps/web/src/lib/effect/session-service.ts](mdc:apps/web/src/lib/effect/session-service.ts)
- Zustand's [apps/web/src/stores/player-prefs-store.ts](mdc:apps/web/src/stores/player-prefs-store.ts) persists preferences only; do not mirror playback or session state there
- Do not introduce Jotai

## Component Structure
- Follow patterns in [apps/web/src/components/media-player/](mdc:apps/web/src/components/media-player/)
- Keep overlay components focused and composable
- Use the established hook patterns from [apps/web/src/components/media-player/hooks/](mdc:apps/web/src/components/media-player/hooks/)

## Video Events
- Use HTML5 video events instead of useEffect for time updates
- Handle video state changes through event listeners
- Follow patterns in [apps/web/src/components/media-player/media-player-video.tsx](mdc:apps/web/src/components/media-player/media-player-video.tsx)

## Plex Integration
- Use existing PlexServerClient methods for media operations
- Follow timeline update patterns from [apps/web/src/components/media-player/hooks/use-timeline-updates.ts](mdc:apps/web/src/components/media-player/hooks/use-timeline-updates.ts)
- Handle play queue operations through established patterns

## Type Safety
- Use types from [apps/web/src/types/media-player.ts](mdc:apps/web/src/types/media-player.ts)
- Extend existing interfaces rather than creating new ones
- Ensure all media player operations are properly typed
